A||||7||Greg Piet||Gas Tank Storage||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||10-09-2000||09:16 PM||||I have a spare gas tank in pretty darn good shape.  It seems like a waste to throw it away.  There is still a small amount of gas in it though(the fuel pump has pumped all it can).  How do I get the rest of gas out of it???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||10-09-2000||10:04 PM||||Turn it upside down?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-09-2000||10:12 PM||||Pour out what you can, the rest should evaporate. Store open to avoid condensation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-09-2000||11:33 PM||||Tie a string to a rag. shove the rag in the tank and let it soak up the liquid that won't pour out.<P>once you've sopped out the liquid leave it <B>outside</B> far from ignition sources untill it dries out the rest. It will dry faster if the fuel pump is also out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||10-10-2000||12:28 AM||||turning it upside down doesnt work (I tried that) with the anti sloshing walls in there.<P>I have been venting it, but with only the filler holes open (I dont want to overwhelm the neighbors)...   <P>the rag thing may do the trick, but then I have to get rig of a gas soaked rag without attracting too much attention.||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||10-10-2000||01:07 PM||||Even with the gas drained out, wouldn't it still smell like gas?  Wouldn't blasting it with a lot of carb cleaner then soaking (or letting evaporate) that out make it smell better in the long run?  Something like that can really smell up a garage. ($0.02) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ed||10-10-2000||07:41 PM||||I hit a rock one time which punctured a car's gas tank.  We took the car to a welding shop to repair the tank.  They seemed to know what to do and not blow themselves up.  <P>So I'd suggest checking the yellow pages for some similar kind of service or knowledge. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||10-10-2000||08:08 PM||||Carb cleaner won't smell any less than the fuel. use the rag trick. squeeze out the rag over a big jar or can. If you get just gas out then put it into another car or a lawn mower or something.<P>Once the rag has sopped out the liquid the rest will dry soon enough. Will dry allot faster with the fuel pump out.||||reg||1
